  "text": "Darren's Thanksgiving glow lasted one day. Tee Higgins missed Friday's practice with what Zac Taylor calls a \"sore\" hamstring, and he is questionable for Sunday against the Saints. Taylor says he is optimistic, which is what coaches say right up until they aren't. The Bengals line slipped from -10 to -9.5 the same day Higgins went on the report, and my read is that the market blinked at that hamstring. Rob, sitting on 31% in that bet, shouldn't start celebrating, because his Chiefs have lost Kenneth Walker III to a groin injury. So it's two limping teams in a race. I still take Darren, if only because his limp comes with the Saints on the schedule.\n\nMeanwhile in Baltimore, Marlon Humphrey returns Sunday in Houston, a week after he was benched for running down the city that pays him. Nobody knows what his role will be, and I'm not sure anyone knows what the point is either. The 4-7 Ravens are getting 6.5 points, and they've just lost Nnamdi Madubuike and Vega Ioane. Rob and Darren co-own this team against Andy and Steve, which is about like splitting a mortgage on a condemned building.\n\nRashee Rice's catch has company on the grievance wall. The Lions are fuming about Bears tackle Jeffery Simmons, who got singled out in the league's officiating video over false starts in Thursday's game. Andy is 95% against Darren and 62% against Steve, so he can afford to sulk. Steve should know that the bookies have quietly shortened the Chiefs to +900. Somebody still believes in them.",
